# What the study of earlier restarts and the greenfield carrier (study/r2/gap-earlier-rewrites.md) found. Sources are under 2.21; the carrier's files are 2.1.8 and 2.1.9; a commit of the old body is cited as 2.1#<hash>.

n: 3.13
name: earlier-restarts-and-carrier
kind: hub
is: Of five sibling checkouts of the old body, one was a restart: a C rewrite of the seed (2026-11-06 to 11-08) that grew from 1,574 lines and 24 operations to 10,302 and 254 in 56 hours, stayed about 40 times slower, and landed only its Form half, on the old C. The other restart is on main: a 1,199-line carrier written from the axioms (2026-11-05). It passes 31 checks on arm64, has no reader or image source, and its store fills after 3,947 offers. About 460 of its lines can be kept; a standalone C bootstrap is estimated at 1,800 to 2,200 lines.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-earlier-rewrites

n: 3.13.1
name: attempts
kind: hub
is: The five sibling checkouts are worktrees of one repository. One held a restart: a C rewrite of the seed that grew 6.5 times in 56 hours while covering the old surface again, stayed about 40 times slower, and landed only its Form half on the old C as one 200-file commit. A second witness for a rewritten runtime was built eight hours after the rewrite began. The study names six causes of not carrying.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-earlier-rewrites

